+# Add t and validate PlaceBlock arguments with it
+
+## Summary
+
+- Adds the [t](https://github.com/osyrisrblx/t) runtime type checker (`osyrisrblx/t`, pinned to
+  `=3.1.1`, the latest on the Wally index) to `pesde.toml` under the alias `t`. It installs
+  through pesde's Wally support like the other packages, into `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t`.
+- Switches the `PlaceBlock` handler in `src/ServerScriptService/BlockPlacement.server.luau` to a
+  single t check, `checkPlaceBlockArgs`, built once at load.
+- Lists t in the README's package table.
+
+## Checks kept
+
+Every argument check the handler made before is still made, now inside `checkPlaceBlockArgs`:
+
+| Before | Now |
+|---|---|
+| `typeof(blockTypeName) ~= "string"` | `t.string` |
+| `BlockTypes.ByName[blockTypeName]` is nil | `t.keyOf(BlockTypes.ByName)` |
+| `typeof(position) ~= "Vector3"` | `t.Vector3` |
+| `position ~= position` (a NaN component) | `isNotNaN`, a custom check combined with `t.Vector3` (t's `Vector3` checks only the type) |
+
+The checks after argument validation (rate limit, character and `HumanoidRootPart`, cell below
+Y = 0 or already occupied, reach) don't change. Any argument that fails a check is still dropped
+without a reply.
+
+## Before testing
+
+`pesde.lock` is **not** updated in this PR: no install was run while it was written.
+
+1. Stop `rojo serve` if it is running.
+2. From the repo root, run `pesde install`. This installs t into `roblox_packages` and updates
+   `pesde.lock`.
+3. Commit the updated `pesde.lock` to this branch. Its diff should add only the
+   `osyrisrblx/t@3.1.1` entry.
+4. Confirm that `roblox_packages/t.luau` exists, then restart `rojo serve` and reconnect the Rojo
+   plugin.
+5. Regenerate the sourcemap so luau-lsp sees the new package:
+   `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts`.
+
+Without the install, the handler errors on `require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t)` at server start.
+
+## Test plan
+
+- [ ] `luau-lsp analyze` (command in the README), `selene src`, and `stylua --check src` pass.
+      selene and stylua already pass on the changed script. luau-lsp has not been run, because it
+      needs the installed package.
+- [ ] Playtest: placing each block type from the client still places a block.
+- [ ] During a playtest, run `ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer(blockType, position)` from
+      the client's command bar with each bad input below. Each one should place nothing and log
+      no error:
+  - a non-string block type (`123`, `nil`)
+  - an unknown block type name (`"Lava"`)
+  - a non-Vector3 position (`"0,0,0"`, `CFrame.new()`)
+  - a NaN position (`Vector3.new(0/0, 4, 0)`)
+- [ ] Rate limit, reach, occupied-cell, and below-ground placements are still rejected.
+
+🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
